From: Verm <183540171+vermingov@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:27:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] feat(linux): load the extension channel into profiles'
 web processes

Each persistent profile's WebKitGTK context gets the web-process plugin
from <binary>/../lib/app.zephium/webext before its first web process, and
each new process gets the profile's enabled extensions. Every view hands
the plugin's messages to the profile's channel, which checks the size, the
format and that the extension is enabled again before anything acts on
them, and answers every message, refused ones too. Private profiles get no
plugin, as upstream runs no extensions there. A missing plugin, or a
directory holding anything else, leaves extensions off.

The .deb carries the plugin, built after the frontend by
desktop/linux/build-webext-plugin.sh. The plugin no longer wraps a missing
reply parameter in a Variant.
